{
  "_comment": "RTDB tunnel cryptography. shared = X25519(viewer_eph, host_eph) (the RFC 7748 6.1 pair). k_dir = HKDF-SHA256(ikm = shared, salt = UTF-8(conn_id), info = UTF-8(\"lingxi-rc-tunnel/1 \" + dir), 32 bytes). A frame is stored as b64u(AES-256-GCM(k_dir, nonce, plaintext, aad) = ciphertext || 16-byte tag) under key \"f\" + decimal seq; nonce = 4 zero bytes || u64 big-endian seq; aad = UTF-8(\"lingxi-rc-tunnel/1\\n\" + conn_id + \"\\n\" + dir + \"\\n\" + seq). plaintext = repeated [u32 big-endian length][fragment], at most 49136 bytes. \"large_frames\" are given as recipes (fragment kind, payload length, fill byte) and checked by length and SHA-256. A frame whose plaintext holds no fragments is the close notice: the sender writes it after its last data frame and then deletes its direction's node; the receiver closes (peer_closed) once it has processed every earlier frame. \"open_failures\" are stored values that must fail authentication under k_up for the given conn_id, dir and seq. \"unpack_failures\" are plaintexts that must be rejected: either {plaintext_hex}, or {fragments: [{length, fill_hex}]} = each fragment is length copies of the fill byte, written with its length prefix. Generated by test/gen-remote-fixtures.mjs.",
